  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The MEX of an array of integers is defined to be the smallest **non-negative integer** not present in it.\n\nFor example, MEX([2,3,1,2])=0\\text{MEX}([2, 3, 1, 2]) = 0MEX([2,3,1,2])=0 and MEX([2,0,3])=1\\text{MEX}([2, 0, 3]) = 1MEX([2,0,3])=1.\n\nYou are given two arrays AAA and BBB, both of length NNN.\n\nYou can perform the following operation on the arrays:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N), and swap AiA_iAi​ with BiB_iBi​.\nFind the minimum possible value of max⁡(MEX(A),MEX(B))\\max(\\text{MEX}(A), \\text{MEX}(B))max(MEX(A),MEX(B)) if you are allowed to perform as many operations as you like (possibly, none).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the arrays.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the answer: the minimum possible value of max⁡(MEX(A),MEX(B))\\max(\\text{MEX}(A), \\text{MEX}(B))max(MEX(A),MEX(B)) after performing some swaps.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤3⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 3\\cdot 10^51≤N≤3⋅105",
      "0≤Ai,Bi&lt;N0 \\leq A_i, B_i \\lt N0≤Ai​,Bi​&lt;N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 3⋅1053\\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
